        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current-state mapping and target payroll workflow design.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 107378,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the 'Standardise Payroll and Office Documentation Workflow' project. To get started on T1, can everyone please share their understanding of the current payroll processing steps? From when you receive a timesheet or a form to the final payment confirmation. Let's map out the as-is process to find the bottlenecks.",
            "mentions": [
              319449,
              330756,
              408577,
              421608
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 421608,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "For me it starts when I get the final numbers to calculate wages and taxes. Then I prepare the statements and send them for approval.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 408577,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Right, but before that, we have to collect all the timesheets and absence forms, check them for manager signatures, and enter any overtime. That part can be slow if forms are missing information.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 319449,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Exactly. From the office clerk side, we receive those forms and route them. A major bottleneck is inconsistent formats and knowing who to send what to, especially for urgent corrections. My experience in payroll showed me that this handoff is where most errors start. We spend a lot of time chasing down the right person.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 330756,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Yes, sometimes I'm not sure if a form goes to payroll directly or to HR first. A clear rule would help.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 107378,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Great points. I've started a draft of the end-to-end workflow in A1 based on this. Here's a proposed sequence: 1. Document Intake (Office Clerks) -> 2. Data Entry & Validation (Payroll) -> 3. Pre-calculation Review -> 4. Tax & Wage Calculation -> 5. Final Approval (Finance Manager) -> 6. Payment Processing -> 7. Archiving. How does that look?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 319449,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "This is a solid foundation. I'd suggest adding a specific 'Discrepancy Resolution' sub-step within 'Data Entry & Validation'. If we don't formalize that, it becomes a bottleneck later. Also, for step 7, 'Archiving' should be owned by both teams for their respective documents to ensure nothing is lost.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 408577,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "I like that addition. Having a formal resolution step will make the monthly close checklist for T3 much easier to manage.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 107378,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Excellent point, I've updated A1 with that sub-step. Okay, let's formalize this. Can we agree on this updated sequence of steps for the standard payroll workflow?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
